      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I see what you did there. You flagged Post 1 as \"promoting violence\" because of the slang (\"trippin\", \"hood\"), but Post 1 is really just someone expressing frustration about local politics or community issues. It's not a call to arms. \n\nCompare that to Post 2. It's framed as a \"statistical observation\" and doesn't use a single slur or aggressive word, yet you flagged it as a failure. \n\nDon't you think the model is being a bit too sensitive to certain dialects? If we use these results to train our filters, we're basically going to end up shadowbanning anyone who uses AAVE or casual slang, while letting people hide actual prejudice behind \"polite\" or \"academic\" language. Can you re-evaluate Post 1 and Post 2? Be more precise about whether they actually violate the rules or if you're just reacting to the tone/dialect.",
